## 🛠️ Technology Stack

| Layer | Technologies |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React, JavaScript |
| UI Components | Material UI (MUI) |
| Routing | React Router |
| HTTP Requests | Axios |
| Backend | Python, Flask |
| Database | SQLite |
| ORM | Flask-SQLAlchemy |
| AI Integration | Google Gemini API |
| Video Recommendations | YouTube Data API |
| Authentication | JWT, Flask-Bcrypt |
| Markdown Rendering | React Markdown, remark-gfm |
| Frontend Tooling | Vite, npm |
| Document Processing | Python libraries configured in the backend |

---

## 🏗️ System Architecture

EduPilot follows a client-server architecture. The React frontend communicates with a Flask backend, which coordinates application logic, database operations, document processing, and configured external services.

### Architecture Flowchart

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    U["Student / User"]

    subgraph F["Frontend — React + Vite"]
        UI["Learning Interface"]
        AUTH["Login and Registration"]
        DASH["Learning Dashboard"]
        NOTES["Notes and Summaries"]
        QUIZ["Quizzes and Flashcards"]
        CHAT["AI Study Chatbot"]
        PLAN["Study Planner"]
        ANALYSIS["Learning Analysis"]
    end

    subgraph B["Backend — Python + Flask"]
        API["Flask API"]
        SEC["Authentication and Validation"]
        LOGIC["Application Logic"]
        DOC["Document Processing"]
        CONTENT["Learning Content Services"]
    end

    subgraph D["Data Layer"]
        ORM["SQLAlchemy ORM"]
        DB[("SQLite Database")]
    end

    GEMINI["Google Gemini API"]
    YOUTUBE["YouTube Data API"]

    U --> UI
    UI --> AUTH
    UI --> DASH
    DASH --> NOTES
    DASH --> QUIZ
    DASH --> CHAT
    DASH --> PLAN
    DASH --> ANALYSIS

    AUTH --> API
    NOTES --> API
    QUIZ --> API
    CHAT --> API
    PLAN --> API
    ANALYSIS --> API

    API --> SEC
    SEC --> LOGIC
    LOGIC --> DOC
    LOGIC --> CONTENT
    LOGIC <--> ORM
    ORM <--> DB

    CONTENT <--> GEMINI
    CONTENT <--> YOUTUBE
    DOC --> CONTENT
```
---

### Architecture Components

- Frontend: Manages screens, user interactions, and API requests.
- Backend: Handles requests, authentication, validation, and learning workflows.
- Learning services: Coordinate configured AI tasks and document processing.
- Database: Persists supported user records, saved sessions, quiz attempts, and study-plan entries.
- External integrations: Provide AI-generated content and video recommendations where configured.

The diagram represents the logical architecture. Exact routes, database relationships, and integrations depend on the current implementation.

